WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.200
Two shorter rules now.

2
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.525
Rule twenty-eight is International only.

3
00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:14.550
A vessel constrained by her draft may show, along with her ordinary power-driven lights, three all-round red lights in a vertical line.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.850
By day, a cylinder.

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.900
You met her on the ladder in lesson seven.

6
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:26.050
And you’ll never see those lights on Inland waters, because that category doesn’t exist there.

7
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.025
Rule twenty-nine is the pilot boat.

8
00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:36.225
A pilot vessel on pilotage duty shows two all-round lights at or near the masthead: white over red.

9
00:00:36.475 --> 00:00:38.850
White over red, pilot ahead.

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.250
Underway, she adds sidelights and a sternlight.

11
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.400
At anchor, she keeps the white over red and adds her anchor light or lights.

12
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:53.600
And when she’s not on pilotage duty, she shows only the ordinary lights for a vessel of her length.

13
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.050
Now be careful with the rhymes, because two of them are mirror images.

14
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.475
White over red is a pilot.

15
00:01:01.725 --> 00:01:03.850
Red over white is fishing.

16
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.975
So ask yourself which color is on top.
